 "title": "More Than Curious: A Science Memoir",
 "byline": "William H. Press \u00b7 Darwin-Finch Publishing, 2023 (Creative Commons)",
 "note": "A memoir, not a textbook: its 70 short chapters are grouped here into eight periods of the author\u2019s life, which are our grouping, not the book\u2019s. Summaries stick to the science, institutions and public events described. Summaries are in our own words; the text stays in the PDF.",
 "summary": "The memoir of astrophysicist and computational scientist William Press, co-author of Numerical Recipes, told through people and institutions he saw up close. It runs from his family\u2019s \u00e9migr\u00e9 roots and a Caltech-faculty childhood in Altadena, through Harvard, weapons-lab summers at Livermore with Edward Teller, and graduate work at Caltech with Kip Thorne on black holes and gravitational waves alongside Feynman and Chandrasekhar; then Princeton, a long Harvard career as astronomy chair and in JASON defense advising, the making of Numerical Recipes, the shift of science to computing, deputy directorship of Los Alamos during the Wen Ho Lee affair and the Cerro Grande fire, arms-control dialogues, and service on President Obama\u2019s PCAST, ending with the COVID era."
}